On Tue, Aug 5, 2014 at 2:22 PM, J. Kurt Anderson <marimbasfz@gmail.com>
wrote:

> And for that first sentence, would this
>
> pa lo la.iuros. rupnu papicivo lo meryru'u
>
> achieve the intended meaning of "1 [of any given] euros is worth 1.34 [of
> any given] American dollars"?


I guess you mean  "pa lo me la.iuros. cu rupnu papicivo lo meryru'u".

But no, the x2 of rupnu has to be a number and in any case, (integer) outer
quantifiers count true sentences, not euros. That says that when you try
each of the referents of "lo me la iuros" in the x1 of "rupnu", once and
only once you end up with a true sentence.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

